quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  25,68,"And these are the people who do not worship any other god apart from Allah, nor do they kill the soul whose killing without any lawful cause Allah has forbidden, nor do they commit adultery. And whoever does this will receive the punishment due for the sin."
  25,69,"His punishment will be doubled on the Day of Rising and, disgraced and humiliated, he will live in it forever."
  25,70,"But whoever repents and believes and does good deeds, so these are the people whose evil deeds Allah will change into good ones. And Allah is Most Forgiving, Ever-Merciful."
  25,71,"And whoever repents and executes good, so he returns to Allah (the way) returning is due."
  25,72,"And these are the people who do not attend (both verbally and practically) the false and untruthful matters, and when they pass by evil activities, they pass on (observing caution) with utmost nobility and dignity."
  25,73,"And these are the people who, when they are directed and guided by means of Revelations of their Lord, do not fall at them deaf and blind (but reflect on them)."
  25,74,"And these are the people who submit (before the presence of Allah): ‘O our Lord, grant us coolness of eyes in our wives and our children, and make us leaders of the Godfearing people.’"
  25,75,They will be rewarded with lofty palaces (in Paradise) as recompense for their patience and steadfastness and will be welcomed therein with greetings and salutations of peace.
  25,76,They will live therein forever. Those (lofty palaces in Paradise) are the most excellent lodgings and (decent) abodes.
  25,77,Say: ‘My Lord cares little for you if you do not worship (Him). But you have indeed rejected (Him). So now this (denial) will ever endure as a permanent torment (for you).’
